WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.450
By most accounts, Benedict Cumberbatch is
a pretty perfect Doctor Strange — but if

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.370
he didn't work his magic, the role could've
been taken by a number of other actors.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.250
In fact, because Cumberbatch declined his
first shot to star in Doctor Strange due to

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.390
scheduling conflicts, director Scott Derrickson
actually met with a number of other potential

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.220
Masters of the Mystic Arts.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.869
Eventually, Derrickson persuaded Marvel to
delay production to accommodate his star,

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:24.240
and the rest is Sorcerer Supreme history.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.310
But who were the other actors who were almost
cast in Doctor Strange?

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.560
Joaquin Phoenix

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.610
As far back as 2014, Marvel pursued Hollywood
weirdo Joaquin Phoenix for the part of Doctor

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.610
Strange.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.149
Contract negotiations were reportedly close
to agreement, but Phoenix is said to have

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:42.989
balked at how much time and creative energy
starring in the movie would consume, not to

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:46.990
mention the appearances in other MCU releases
that he'd be obligated to make over the next

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:47.990
few years.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:51.700
He ultimately decided he preferred indie efforts
to superhero blockbusters.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.260
As Vanity Fair once pointed out when Phoenix
was rumored for the role of Lex Luthor,

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.719
"Do you really expect the guy who seems actively
miserable any time he has to leave his house

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:02.940
to take on a movie that requires a visit to
Comic-Con?"

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.019
Ryan Gosling

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:07.960
According to The Guardian, after Joaquin Phoenix
turned down Doctor Strange, Ryan Gosling took

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.860
some meetings with Marvel Studios.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.560
At the same time, he was also being considered
for a role in Suicide Squad.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.810
Maybe to play a Joker who didn't send dead
rats to his castmates?

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.439
And in a 2014 interview that year, Gosling
hinted he'd also love to play the Flash for

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:22.439
DC.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:26.310
Unfortunately for fans of costumed "Hey Girl"
memes, he ultimately didn't land any of these

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.310
parts.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.770
But there are still plenty of potential roles
to go 'round.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.570
Goslactus, anyone?

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:32.950
Jared Leto

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.520
Director Scott Derrickson told Empire that
when it looked like Cumberbatch was a no-go,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:41.540
he met with "a lot of good actors," including
Jared Leto, hot off his Best Supporting Actor

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.020
win for Dallas Buyers Club.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.180
As we all know, Leto would eventually make
his mark in the comic movie world in Suicide

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.500
Squad… for a full seven minutes of screen
time, before later asking for the release

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.320
of unseen x-rated footage that he apparently
shot.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.880
Ultimately, this dude would've brought a level
of strange that the Doctor definitely didn't

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.880
need.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:00.880
Ethan Hawke

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.700
While doing promotion for his Oscar-nominated
turn in Boyhood, Ethan Hawke mentioned on

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.219
a podcast that he came "as close as anybody
could" to playing Stephen Strange.

00:02:09.219 --> 00:02:13.469
Hawke suspected he didn't land the part because
he doesn't have a huge fanbase like Benedict

00:02:13.469 --> 00:02:16.650
Cumberbatch, nor is he a major box office
draw, saying,

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.860
"If people are gonna put up with somebody
like me, they wanna make sure you're gonna

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:25.049
put asses in seats, and there's a lot of actors
that are gonna put more asses in seats than

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:26.049
me."

00:02:26.049 --> 00:02:27.049
He's...not wrong.

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:32.569
"Ethan Hawke seems like a guy who wasn't supposed
to be a movie star, but he slipped through

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:36.800
the cracks and everyone was just like 'Ok.'"

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:37.859
Ewan McGregor

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:41.810
No stranger to the weird ways of the universe,
there was apparently mutual interest between

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.879
Marvel and Ewan McGregor for Doctor Strange.

00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:48.390
In 2015, a reporter from MTV asked McGregor
about his involvement in the movie.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:54.940
"I was intrigued by it and I like the idea
of creating a superhero character."

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:55.940
"Ya."

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.940
"Why wouldn't you?"

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.170
Despite his serious nerd credibility, McGregor
believes his lack of comic knowledge bumped

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.900
him out of the running for the role, but said
"it was still fun to be a part of the mix

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:04.900
for a while."

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.959
But really, you can't have Star Wars and Marvel.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:09.359
That would just be greedy.

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:10.730
Patrick Dempsey

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:14.349
A movie star in the '80s, Patrick Dempsey
enjoyed a massive comeback when he took on

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:18.999
a starring role on ABC's popular soap Grey's
Anatomy in 2005.

00:03:18.999 --> 00:03:22.189
In 2011, he admitted he was looking to get
back into movies, specifically with a movie

00:03:22.189 --> 00:03:24.359
adaptation of Doctor Strange.

00:03:24.359 --> 00:03:27.419
Dempsey publicly discussed his attraction
to the character with the Los Angeles Times,

00:03:27.419 --> 00:03:28.419
saying,

00:03:28.419 --> 00:03:29.419
"I've been lobbying for that.

00:03:29.419 --> 00:03:30.419
It would be fantastic.

00:03:30.419 --> 00:03:33.650
It'd be a great TV show, especially for HBO
or something like that."

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.250
Marvel obviously envisioned the Doctor on
a bigger screen, and Dempsey wasn't part of

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.290
the picture.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.290
Nicolas Cage

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:44.480
Director/writer Roman Coppola is part of the
unstoppable Coppola filmmaking dynasty.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.389
Years ago, before the Marvel Cinematic Universe
was a thing, Coppola set out to make his own

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:50.019
version of Doctor Strange.

00:03:50.019 --> 00:03:54.140
At the time, the comic was still just a cult
favorite, but after a chance meeting with

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:58.839
Stan Lee, and seeing how terrible The Fantastic
Four was, Coppola was inspired.

00:03:58.839 --> 00:04:02.559
Coppola says he spent a while planning it,
and he even had an actor in mind for the role

00:04:02.559 --> 00:04:06.669
of Doctor Strange: his cousin, the actually
strange Nicolas Cage.

00:04:06.669 --> 00:04:08.919
"I'm like a prickly pear!"

00:04:08.919 --> 00:04:13.629
Though after seeing how Cage handled Marvel's
Ghost Rider — twice — it's probably best

00:04:13.629 --> 00:04:14.629
he didn't get the role.

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:19.560
Now in his 50s, it might be too late for comic
nerd Cage to grab ahold of another superhero

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.560
part.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.560
"Too late!

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.560
Too late!

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.560
Too late!"

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.560
Thanks for watching!

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.270
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.889
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

